--TEST--
A `Core\Fatal::onUncaughtThrow` handler that throws is abandoned where it stands, is not entered a second time, and does not become the failure the engine reports — `rule:errors/on-uncaught-throw` and `rule:errors/handler-script`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// § 2's "same zero-retry rule", asked at the boundary that makes it observable:
// the handler throws, and the throw it was called *about* is still the one the
// floor reports on standard error below. A ladder that let the reporter's own
// failure replace the request's would print `the reporter failed too` there,
// which is the failure mode worth being loud about — the original error would
// be gone and the log would name the log handler.
Core\Fatal::onUncaughtThrow(fn (Throwable $seen): void => {
    echo "handler entered for: ", $seen->message, "\n";
    throw new RuntimeError("the reporter failed too");
});

// Nor is it re-entered. The registration is taken out of the slot on the way
// in (`Ctx::run_uncaught_handler`), so the handler's own uncaught throw finds
// nothing to fire and the count of lines above is one — a ladder that re-armed
// the slot instead prints two and then keeps going.
echo "start\n";
throw new LogicError("boom");
--EXPECT--
start
handler entered for: boom
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
{"level":"error","msg":"boom","fields":{"class":"LogicError"},"nodes":%s}
